// AXVERITY_EXTENT_WRITE_PATH step 2/3 — the coordinator's queue. TWO
// producers (mem_controller's write bundles, the tick thread's SLA ticks),
// ONE consumer (disk_controller). Messages are [0] for a tick and
// [1, <bundle>] for a write: the kind leads so the bundle travels nested and
// byte-identical to what mem_controller built, leaving flusher untouched.
// One queue rather than two channels is what makes a single blocking take
// sufficient — no non-blocking take exists in M1, and none is needed.
channel wp-dc
  type Value
end

// AXVERITY_EXTENT_WRITE_PATH step 2 — one-shot handoff of the run cell to the
// tick thread. The tick loop is the pipeline's only unbounded loop; this cell
// is how it learns the run has ended. A cell rather than a channel because the
// timer must ask "still running?" WITHOUT blocking.
channel wp-run-cell-pub
  type Value
end

